1
00:00:07,966 --> 00:00:11,720
LITTLE MISS U '99

2
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:14,473
[announcer in English]
Let's welcome Joanna Celis!

3
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:18,060
[singing in Filipino]
♪ Why do I love you so ♪

4
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:19,520
♪ Even though ♪

5
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:21,855
♪ You're in love with someone else? ♪

6
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,691
So you want to be an actress?

7
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,151
Yes, sir.

8
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:27,778
Do you know how to act?

9
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:30,781
- No, sir.
- ♪ Why do I love you so ♪

10
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:32,741
♪ Even though ♪

11
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:35,160
♪ You're in love with someone else? ♪

12
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:36,828
♪ Why am I so crazy about you... ♪

13
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:39,540
[Willie] Today's Little Miss U

14
00:00:39,623 --> 00:00:41,667
with an average score
of 90 percent...

15
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:44,127
- Candidate number three...
- [Randy] Three.

16
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,712
- [Willie] ...Joanna Celis!
- [Randy] Joanna.

17
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,465
[engine revs]

18
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:49,716
[Chin] Hello, Sir Gab.

19
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,219
Please tell my family
that I love them all so much.

20
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,762
Please do that for me, Sir Gab.

21
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:55,847
[tense music]

22
00:00:57,391 --> 00:00:59,184
What are you talking about?
I'm already in Taguig.

23
00:00:59,268 --> 00:01:00,269
I won't be long now.

24
00:01:00,352 --> 00:01:01,770
- Hail Mary, full of grace...
- [Gab] Chin.

25
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:02,854
Are you okay?

26
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:04,106
Will we make it?

27
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,483
Yeah, we'll make it. Chin?

28
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:09,403
[grunts]
I think this is the end for me.

29
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:10,529
You can do this, go on.

30
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,030
Come quickly, Sir Gab!

31
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,117
I'll be quick, I'm so close.

32
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,578
I can't do this. They'll kill me!

33
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:19,413
Just get to our meeting place.

34
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:21,748
- [Chin] Now?
- Yes, right now!

35
00:01:21,832 --> 00:01:23,417
I'll try.

36
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,168
You sound like you're in a well.

37
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:27,087
- [Gab] Hey!
- [Mrs. Celis] Son of a gun!

38
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,171
- [Gab] Sorry!
- Gab!

39
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,091
- Sorry.
- [car horn honks]

40
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,175
[Gab] Move!

41
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,177
What's going on?

42
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:35,887
- [Mrs. Celis] What, is she sleeping?
- [Gab] Hey!

43
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:37,389
- [thuds]
- [exclaims]

44
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,684
- [Mrs. Celis] What's happening?
- Chin!

45
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:43,520
Chin?

46
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:46,023
[producer] Darn it, Chin!

47
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:51,278
Chin!

48
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:54,531
Chin!

49
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:57,075
[tires screech]

50
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,873
[comical music]

51
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:06,376
- Excuse us. Coming through. Thanks!
- [man 1] What's that?

52
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,587
- [Gab] Mommy, watch out for the kid.
- [Mrs. Celis] Oh, my.

53
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:09,713
Hey there.

54
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:11,840
[crew] Shut the lights.

55
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,091
- [Gab] Where are they?
- [crew] She's not here yet.

56
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:14,885
- [Chin] Wait!
- [crew] Have your dinner break.

57
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:17,054
- [Chin] Sir Gab.
- [Gab] Coming through, please.

58
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,056
- Who's this?
- [Chin] It's me, Chin!

59
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:21,183
[Gab] Chin! Let's go! Hurry!

60
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,351
[Mrs. Celis] Oh, hey, Chin!

61
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,146
[Gab] Excuse me.

62
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,023
Careful, guys. It's really tight.

63
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:30,901
Careful now, Mommy!

64
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,402
[Chin exclaims]

65
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,154
[Chin] Darn it.

66
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,825
- Chin! Turn off the light.
- [Chin] Here you go.

67
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,828
- What happened anyway?
- [Mrs. Celis] Hurry up!

68
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:43,872
Did you go shopping in BGC?

69
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:47,084
The music video just wrapped up.

70
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,585
- [light switch clicks]
- Hey!

71
00:02:48,669 --> 00:02:50,420
- [Gab] Shut the lights! Please!
- [crew] What...

72
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:52,047
- I'm so sorry.
- [Chin] Thank you.

73
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,757
The director is ready for Kiray.

74
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,884
We're coming, thank you!

75
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:58,470
[Chin] Didn't we pass on that gig?

76
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,846
You couldn't resist, Mommy?

77
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,432
- I didn't want to waste the gig!
- [light switch clicks]

78
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,184
- [in angry voice] Hey!
- Will you shut the lights?

79
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,061
- Oh, hello, ma'am.
- Hello.

80
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:07,145
She owns this house.

81
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:09,231
- [in calm voice] Oh, hello, Grandma.
- Hi, ma'am.

82
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:10,691
- Turn off the lights!
- Apologies.

83
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:11,817
Sorry. Thank you.

84
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,360
[Gab] Take care of this, Chin, okay?

85
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,444
[Chin] All right.

86
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:16,530
- Can you just shut the darn lights?
- [Mrs. Celis] Come on!

87
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:17,614
[producer] Okay.

88
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:20,242
[crew] Everyone standby! Ready!

89
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:26,581
[clatters]

90
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:28,291
- [Gab] Ms. Dindin!
- What the heck, Gab?

91
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:29,710
- Hello!
- It's been three hours!

92
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:31,086
We've been waiting for so long.

93
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,921
- I've run out of excuses!
- I know!

94
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:34,172
Right, and I'm here to explain...

95
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:35,966
- What happened was...
- Where's your road manager?

96
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,551
Where is that Chin-Chin?

97
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,886
- Chin.
- I've been looking for him!

98
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,304
That road manager is utterly useless!

99
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:44,558
Let me explain. Well, you see,
the other shoot went into overtime...

100
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:46,268
- I don't care!
- It rained and...

101
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:49,354
I don't care even if aliens
or whatever attacked you.

102
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:51,523
The meter is running here, Gabriel!

103
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:52,691
- I know, but...
- You know what?

104
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:55,110
This is the last time.

105
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:56,278
No, Ms. Dindin!

106
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,447
- I'm never hiring her again.
- No, please!

107
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,282
- And that freaking mother of hers...
- No!

108
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:02,993
...who'll hijack this ad
if we let her!

109
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,661
- I understand!
- [producer] This is too much!

110
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:06,496
- No, let me explain...
- [Kiray] Hello, everyone!

111
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,623
Hello! Hi!

112
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,710
- There she is.
- Kiray!

113
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,920
[producer] Hello!

114
00:04:14,004 --> 00:04:15,922
- [Kiray] Hello!
- [producer] Kiray!

115
00:04:16,006 --> 00:04:18,717
- Hello!
- Hello!

116
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,470
Finally, you are here.

117
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,305
Here's coffee.

118
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:25,390
- Have some coffee.
- That's nice.

119
00:04:25,474 --> 00:04:26,767
- Okay, let's go.
- All right.

120
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:28,810
And Mommy Celis,
looking gorgeous as always!

121
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:30,145
[crew] Bubbles test, bubbles test!

122
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:31,521
[reporter] So what's next...

123
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,106
What's next for Kiray, Mommy C?

124
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,233
- You seem to be so busy!
- [Mrs. Celis] Yes.

125
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:38,069
Actually, we just finished
a music video.

126
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:40,155
- [reporter] And what else?
- [Mrs. Celis] And now this.

127
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:42,532
Right? So, Kiray's manager says

128
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:44,409
he has lots of projects
lined up for her.

129
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:46,620
You mean you're not Kiray's manager?

130
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,205
- [reporter] Uh, wait.
- [Mrs. Celis chuckles]

131
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,915
[Mrs. Celis] Not technically,
but I help them out.

132
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:51,416
- I'm like a co-manager.
- [phone ringing]

133
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,168
- [in English] Hey, Kelly!
- [Kelly] Hi, Gabriel.

134
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:54,336
Great news!

135
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:57,130
Everybody is raving
about Kiray's audition

136
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:58,298
for Women in Chains.

137
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:02,427
We saw lots of Filipino actors,
but kept coming back to Kiray.

138
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:03,929
She was that good!

139
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:05,013
And?

140
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,765
[Kelly] She got the part!

141
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,600
That's great news!

142
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:10,519
Thank you, thank you!

143
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:13,230
Perfect choice,
you won't regret this.

144
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:15,398
Thank you! Thank you, Kelly.

145
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:17,442
[Kelly] Oh, it's all Kiray.

146
00:05:17,526 --> 00:05:20,028
Now, as soon as she gets
those surgeries

147
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:22,614
we can fly her out here
to meet the rest of the cast.

148
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:23,865
That's awesome.

149
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,409
She'll be very excited
to meet everyone.

150
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:28,870
Wait.

151
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:30,539
Wait.

152
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:32,040
What surgeries?

153
00:05:33,124 --> 00:05:34,376
We're still doing the surgeries?

154
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:37,295
Look, if you need me
to talk to the parents, I'll do it.

155
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:40,257
[Gab] But she's only 18 years old.

156
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,341
Eighteen?

157
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,385
You told me she was 21!

158
00:05:43,552 --> 00:05:46,888
Yeah, that's what I meant, 21.

159
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:48,807
18, 21, she's an adult.

160
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:52,018
[Kelly] Look, they may still change
the title of the film.

161
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:55,105
I'm gonna send you the email
and the sizes we're looking at.

162
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,023
Sizes?

163
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:59,734
[clicking]

164
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,152
[Kelly] Look, Gabriel.

165
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:04,114
This is Quentin's favorite
Eddie Romero film.

166
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:06,700
He's been wanting to do
a Hollywood remake

167
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,326
of this movie for years

168
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:09,786
with a Filipino actor.

169
00:06:10,287 --> 00:06:11,663
That could be Kiray!

170
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,125
But only if she has the surgeries!

171
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:18,712
This is gonna make her
an international artist!

172
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,755
The biggest decision of her life!

173
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:23,091
Kiray can hold her own
in the acting department.

174
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:24,676
She's going to be massive.

175
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:27,137
Biggest opportunity of her career.

176
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,722
It's an enormous chance!

177
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:29,973
Can we just get this done?

178
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:32,142
When this film is a huge success

179
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,352
you can rub it in everybody's faces.

180
00:06:34,436 --> 00:06:35,478
Do you understand?

181
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:36,897
She's gonna take off after this.

182
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,149
But only if she has the surgeries!

183
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,442
[echoes] Surgeries...

184
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,611
It's a humongous opportunity!

185
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:43,737
You've got to grab it.

186
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:44,905
Grab it! Grab it! Grab it!

187
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:46,072
[director] Cut!

188
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:49,159
[theme music]

189
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,829
♪ Careful, careful ♪

190
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:56,791
♪ The world is full
Of jealous people ♪

191
00:06:56,875 --> 00:07:00,003
♪ When envy strikes,
It means trouble♪

192
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:02,213
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

193
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:04,341
♪ Careful, careful ♪

194
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:08,345
♪ We always need to be careful ♪

195
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:11,348
♪ Prying eyes ready to snoop ♪

196
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:14,559
♪ Digging for the juiciest scoop ♪

197
00:07:14,643 --> 00:07:17,145
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

198
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,651
♪ Careful, careful ♪

199
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:28,323
[train horn honks]

200
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:31,159
[thrilling music]

201
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,630
[indistinct chatter]

202
00:07:45,548 --> 00:07:46,591
[Matthew] Noemi?

203
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,052
Noemi?

204
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:51,888
Noemi, where are you?

205
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,349
[in English] Shine Artist Management,
how can I help you?

206
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:55,850
[in Filipino]
Noemi, where is the contract?

207
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,019
And Director Richard's script?

208
00:07:58,645 --> 00:07:59,729
Sir Matthew.

209
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,191
Let's go. Take everything with you.

210
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,442
[in English] I'm coming, sir.

211
00:08:05,110 --> 00:08:06,444
I'll give you an update later today.

212
00:08:06,528 --> 00:08:07,862
[Andrea]
Did you get any sleep at all?

213
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:09,155
- [Addy] Not really.
- [Andrea] Good.

214
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:11,074
We're visiting Nadine on set.

215
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,242
Right. 2:00 p.m.

216
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,702
Then we'll pick up Elisse.

217
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,412
- Yes, at 4:00 p.m.
- No!

218
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,955
- Switch them.
- Okay.

219
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,248
Nadine is doing a tracking shot.

220
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:20,125
- You're not thinking straight.
- Yes, Ms. Andrea.

221
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,002
[Addy] Oh, about Ms. Janine...

222
00:08:23,712 --> 00:08:24,713
Ms. Andrea.

223
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:26,089
Do you think we'll be back
by 7:00 p.m.?

224
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,257
- Ms. Andrea?
- What?

225
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,967
Ms. Janine is asking for a meeting.

226
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,719
- Janine who?
- Gutierrez.

227
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:31,803
- Gutierrez?
- Yes, ma'am.

228
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,555
- What did you say?
- I said yes.

229
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,973
Oh, my god, why would you do that?

230
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:37,017
You have my schedule, right?
Are you out of your mind?

231
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,560
You know my schedule,
and you said yes?

232
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:40,478
- Take it back!
- She said it was urgent.

233
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,480
My schedule is so full!

234
00:08:42,564 --> 00:08:45,400
[in English] Do something about it!
And I need my coffee!

235
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:47,485
I get it. Yes.

236
00:08:47,569 --> 00:08:48,987
I understand.

237
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:50,989
Kelly, listen.

238
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:53,491
I don't want to lose this
for her either.

239
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,329
[in Filipino] Hi, I'm here to see...

240
00:08:58,413 --> 00:08:59,998
[in English] Okay.
I'll send it over right away.

241
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,332
Okay, thank you.

242
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,418
Two minutes. Yes?

243
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:06,254
- Matthew Buenaventura, please.
- Sandra?

244
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:10,675
- Margie? Regal Films? Donna?
- [Deo] Cleaning!

245
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:12,886
Ms. Vivian?

246
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,929
Oro Holdings?

247
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,015
Thanks, Sofie!

248
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,600
It's Camille Vergara.

249
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,351
Camille Vergara.

250
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:21,603
A family friend.

251
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,563
Family friend.
Oh, my god, he's very busy.

252
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:25,774
[in Filipino] He can't meet anyone
without an appointment.

253
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:28,651
[in English] Shine Artist Management,
how may I help you?

254
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:32,197
[in Filipino]
You want to be an actress, right?

255
00:09:32,614 --> 00:09:36,326
Just leave your resume and set cards.

256
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:37,535
I'm not an actress.

257
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:40,830
Miss, everybody wants to be a star.

258
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:44,417
- [Sofie] Okay, ma'am, yes...
- Is it okay to wait?

259
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,503
Yes, ma'am, bye!

260
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:48,713
Okay, here's what we'll do.

261
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:51,424
Give me an ID
and sign your name here.

262
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,469
I'll give you a visitor's pass.

263
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:57,013
[Sofie] We close at 9:00 p.m.
You can wait over there.

264
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:01,726
Mm...

265
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:10,693
Yeah, it's me, Niño Muhlach.

266
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:13,238
Okay, sir, I see.

267
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:17,075
I was Wonder Boy back in the day.

268
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,494
Child Wonder of Philippine Movies.

269
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:23,665
Maybe you've seen my film Kuwatog?
I played a dwarf.

270
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,584
Actually, that earned 6 million
in Metro Manila alone.

271
00:10:26,668 --> 00:10:30,004
To think movie tickets
only cost 2.50 pesos back then.

272
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:33,591
Or maybe you've seen my film
with Lino Brocka?

273
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,051
Stop Crying, Little Boy?

274
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:39,556
Oh, maybe the one I did with Dolphy?
My Father, My Mother?

275
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:51,484
My manager was Mother Aleta.

276
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:52,694
She's a producer, right?

277
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:53,945
Now, she is.

278
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,822
But back in the day,
she was my manager.

279
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,740
Actually, I was her biggest star.

280
00:10:58,575 --> 00:11:00,285
She's talking to SAM's owner now.

281
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:02,412
Because I'm going to make a comeback.

282
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:09,335
So, where did you recognize me from?

283
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:13,339
[hesitates]
Maybe my grandma would recognize you.

284
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:15,049
[Camille] Excuse me.

285
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,261
- Miss...
- [Sofie] Sofie.

286
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:20,430
Ms. Sofie, can you try Matthew again?

287
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,473
All right, wait, I'll check.

288
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:28,229
- Hello.
- [Sofie] Hi, Sir Matthew.

289
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:30,398
[in English] Um...
Camille Vergara here to see you.

290
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:33,943
Okay.

291
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:35,028
Okay.

292
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:36,529
Okay.

293
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:38,615
Okay, then.

294
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:39,949
Okay, bye.

295
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:43,036
[in Filipino] He's really busy.

296
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,329
Why do you want to speak to him?

297
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,164
- [Deo] Where do these go?
- Oh, my god!

298
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:48,416
Deo, that's a surprise!

299
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,710
[Sofie] We have to keep those hidden!

300
00:11:51,461 --> 00:11:52,462
Matt!

301
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:54,505
I'm gonna grab a bite.

302
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:01,262
[in English] This is not happening.

303
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:03,514
You're not supposed to be here.

304
00:12:03,598 --> 00:12:04,807
[in Filipino] Why are you here?

305
00:12:04,891 --> 00:12:06,142
You want to be an actress
or something?

306
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:09,103
You're the second person
to ask me that.

307
00:12:09,938 --> 00:12:11,356
Maybe I should be an actress.

308
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:14,317
Maybe I can work for you.

309
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,153
[in English] No! That's impossible.

310
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:19,155
That can never happen.

311
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,618
[exhales sharply]

312
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,580
In the meantime,
this will have to do.

313
00:12:29,666 --> 00:12:30,750
[in Filipino] I don't want that.

314
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:33,878
[in English] You said you need work.

315
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:34,963
[in Filipino] I do!

316
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:36,673
[in English] I want to work.

317
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:40,134
Fine! If not for you,
for this agency.

318
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:42,470
[in Filipino]
I always check your social media.

319
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:43,805
I want to work here.

320
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:46,140
I want to earn my own money here.

321
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:48,017
Let's just talk on the phone.

322
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:49,686
[in English] We can't see each other.

323
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:51,813
[in Filipino] Especially not here.

324
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:56,234
I won't tell anyone.

325
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:58,945
[waitress in English]
Hi! Welcome to LibCafé.

326
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:01,406
[in Filipino]
Charge it to the office.

327
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:03,908
You said we're going to grab a bite.

328
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:06,703
[thrilling music]

329
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:09,706
[Addy] I can't do this.

330
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:11,457
This is too much.

331
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:13,751
It's gonna be fine. They're here.

332
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:16,796
Abi!

333
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:17,922
Come here.

334
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:21,676
Enough chit-chat.

335
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:23,303
Make sure the presentation is ready.

336
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:24,554
- Yes, Ms. Andrea.
- [Samuel] Oh!

337
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,888
Look who's here!

338
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,015
[Andrea] Mother!

339
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:29,392
- Hey, how are you?
- Good!

340
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:31,311
- I missed you!
- I missed you, too!

341
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:32,937
- Looking beautiful!
- Thank you!

342
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,272
No need to fuss.

343
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:35,815
I'm not staying long.

344
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:38,151
I'm only here to endorse Niño to you.

345
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:40,111
Can you send in Niño, please?

346
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,738
Which one is he?

347
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,197
[Aleta] Niño Muhlach.

348
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,200
Aga Muhlach's brother?

349
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:47,952
He was in Kuwatog.

350
00:13:48,036 --> 00:13:49,037
My Father, My Mother.

351
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,621
[Matthew] And...

352
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,165
Stop Crying, Little Boy.

353
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:53,666
[in English] Exactly.

354
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,169
[Aleta in Filipino]
That's why I brought him here.

355
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:58,421
He needs to make a comeback.

356
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:02,342
Niño used to be
my biggest moneymaker.

357
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:03,843
- Now that he's old...
- Matt!

358
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,887
- ...he's all yours.
- Matt!

359
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:06,971
Buddy! Oh, here!

360
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,848
I brought you guys some ensaymada.

361
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,641
- Enjoy!
- Thank you!

362
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:11,726
Gabs!

363
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,102
- Bro!
- Bro!

364
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:14,354
- Long time, huh?
- Yup!

365
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:15,855
- How are you?
- Nice to see you.

366
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:17,357
Hello.

367
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:20,401
So, who's Niño's new manager?

368
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:21,903
Uh...

369
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,071
Um...

370
00:14:23,154 --> 00:14:26,324
It should be someone
who can relate to me.

371
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,993
[Niño] Someone who's seen my films.

372
00:14:29,077 --> 00:14:30,620
That's Matthew.

373
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,288
He's a big fan of yours.

374
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,458
- Matthew, take care of Niño, okay?
- Matt!

375
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:36,584
- Matt!
- Of course, Mother.

376
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,252
[in English]
I knew we were meant for each other!

377
00:14:38,336 --> 00:14:40,213
[Aleta in Filipino]
When are you leaving for Germany?

378
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:41,297
- Let's talk.
- Uh...

379
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:42,840
- [Matthew] I'll text you.
- I fly tonight.

380
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:45,593
Are you taking Mrs. Mendiola or...

381
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,220
What's your new woman's name again?

382
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,055
Madel. Her name is Madel.

383
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,139
Hey.

384
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:53,810
- Mother!
- Hmm?

385
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:55,061
Are you jealous?

386
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:58,356
- [playful hooting]
- [laughs]

387
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,816
Let's go, Niño.

388
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,567
They're making fun of me.

389
00:15:01,651 --> 00:15:03,361
- Bye, have a safe trip.
- [Samuel] Okay.

390
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:05,988
- [Aleta] Tata, we're leaving.
- Take care on the trip!

391
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:07,115
- [Samuel] Okay.
- [Niño] Bye!

392
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,035
[Matthew] Samuel.

393
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:12,912
[Samuel] I know, I know.

394
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:15,498
It's hard to get Niño roles.

395
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:17,500
But this is your job.

396
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:20,336
I hired you because you're good.

397
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,504
So be good at this!

398
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:25,133
- Okay. Time for updates!
- [Andrea] Updates!

399
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,926
[Matthew] I just closed...

400
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:29,679
endorsement deals
for Brandon and Jessica.

401
00:15:30,388 --> 00:15:31,389
Two, as a matter of fact.

402
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:34,684
One is sports-related,
and the other is...

403
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:36,853
a lifestyle brand.

404
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,271
[Samuel] Well done!

405
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:39,647
[in English] But make sure

406
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,942
none of this gets in the way
of Juan Makabayan, okay?

407
00:15:43,526 --> 00:15:44,694
I'm serious!

408
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:46,654
[in Filipino] This is huge!

409
00:15:47,155 --> 00:15:48,156
Think about it.

410
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,366
A film shot
in the Philippines and Spain!

411
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:52,368
Have you read the script?

412
00:15:57,707 --> 00:15:58,708
[in English] I did!

413
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,001
[in Filipino] It's great!

414
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,629
A great script! Really great.

415
00:16:04,422 --> 00:16:06,007
[Matthew in English]
It's the rise and fall

416
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,675
of the great Filipino entrepreneur.

417
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:09,218
[in Filipino]
There's action and drama.

418
00:16:09,594 --> 00:16:11,554
There's espionage and sex!

419
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:12,972
[in English] All in one movie.

420
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:15,099
- [in Filipino] This is epic!
- Yeah.

421
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:17,685
Imagine, it spans 50 years.

422
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,604
A ton of big scenes.

423
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:21,189
It's an acting piece!

424
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:25,193
There are good things ahead
for whoever plays Juan Makabayan.

425
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:29,655
I want our talents
to be in this project.

426
00:16:29,739 --> 00:16:33,910
I want the lead actor
to be one of ours, okay?

427
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:35,620
[in English]
I'll take care of that, Samuel.

428
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:38,039
We should all be on top of that.

429
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,875
Because it's a big project.

430
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:44,170
[in Filipino]
We should all work to get this done.

431
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:48,090
I only offered because the producers
are my golfing buddies.

432
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:49,175
Oh, yeah?

433
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:50,843
I don't think golf
can get a film done.

434
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:53,763
Do you?

435
00:16:54,222 --> 00:16:55,389
[in English] Huh? I don't think so.

436
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:03,856
[in Filipino] And Gab and I can help
scout locations in Spain.

437
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:05,650
Why? Because we have lots
of connections there.

438
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:08,611
[Andrea] The production
will appreciate us even more

439
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,238
if we use our connections.

440
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:11,322
Right, Gab?

441
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:14,158
Yes, of course! We can. Absolutely.

442
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:15,743
[in English] Guys, it's confirmed.

443
00:17:16,536 --> 00:17:19,789
Eddie Romero's Women In Chains
is getting a Hollywood remake.

444
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,792
- Wow.
- And our very own

445
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,253
Kiray Celis got the lead part.

446
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,213
[in Filipino] Wow, that's good.

447
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,297
Ooh...

448
00:17:28,381 --> 00:17:30,049
[in sarcastic tone] Hollywood, yay.

449
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,133
Whoo-hoo.

450
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:33,719
[in Filipino] You don't seem happy.

451
00:17:35,346 --> 00:17:38,015
The deal is, Kiray has to get
breast augmentation surgery.

452
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,100
[scoffs]

453
00:17:39,934 --> 00:17:40,935
Chin.

454
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:44,855
- [Samuel] Huh?
- Oh, wow.

455
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:49,151
[Samuel] Whoa, these are huge!

456
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,070
[Gab] I know.

457
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:52,738
I think I'm going to pass.

458
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:54,156
Gab.

459
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:57,034
Why would you pass up

460
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,662
an opportunity this big?

461
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:01,706
[Gab in English] She's only 18.

462
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:03,499
[in unison] Twenty-one.

463
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:04,625
Twenty-one.

464
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:05,793
Okay, 21.

465
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,129
I can't let her do this.

466
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,840
[in Filipino]
She doesn't even know what she wants.

467
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:12,592
She wants to be famous, right?

468
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:15,011
You mean they want to be famous.

469
00:18:16,053 --> 00:18:19,974
Mrs. Celis will go crazy
over her earnings.

470
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:21,183
Good luck telling her

471
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,352
you want to give up that project.
I'm telling you.

472
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:25,521
Fine. I'll find her another one.

473
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:26,772
Other projects.

474
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,650
No, you need
to find her other projects.

475
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:31,986
Okay, other projects, then.

476
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:34,655
Chin is making content

477
00:18:34,739 --> 00:18:37,491
for her social media pages.

478
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:39,744
We'll strengthen her online presence.

479
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:41,537
Gabriel, let me remind you

480
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:43,998
that SAM is in the business
of building stars

481
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:47,001
and not online sensations.

482
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:48,336
Well, actually...

483
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:51,422
So Kiray snagged the role!

484
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:55,384
Janine Gutierrez,
she also auditioned for that role.

485
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,011
But the production said

486
00:18:57,094 --> 00:19:00,056
she was kind of mature for the role.

487
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,974
That's why it went to Kiray.

488
00:19:02,058 --> 00:19:03,351
But it's still SAM.

489
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,186
[Samuel] What do they want,
a toddler?

490
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,438
[Andrea] I know, right? I don't know.

491
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:10,775
But, you know,
I have a ton of projects for Janine.

492
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:13,277
- And I can actually...
- [Addy whispering]

493
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:16,781
Is there something you want to share?

494
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,157
You have been at it the whole time.

495
00:19:18,658 --> 00:19:20,159
[Andrea] You're distracting us.

496
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:22,411
Abi, is there something
you have to say?

497
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:24,038
[in English] Do you want
to share it with us?

498
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:27,667
[in Filipino] Nothing?
So can I continue?

499
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:30,753
[in English] Okay, thank you!

500
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,797
Okay. Going back.

501
00:19:33,381 --> 00:19:35,049
I got two movies for Janine

502
00:19:35,383 --> 00:19:38,678
a product endorsement,
and a possible series for her

503
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:39,929
and there's one more...

504
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:41,013
Abi, what else?

505
00:19:41,097 --> 00:19:42,807
[in Filipino] I'm sure there's more.

506
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,351
There's nothing else.

507
00:19:46,102 --> 00:19:47,269
- Nothing?
- Nothing.

508
00:19:48,062 --> 00:19:50,690
Not a thing.
No series, no movies. Nothing.

509
00:19:50,773 --> 00:19:52,024
No endorsements. None. Zero.

510
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:53,609
Because she's moving
to another agency.

511
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,111
She doesn't want to be here anymore.

512
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:57,738
[nervous chuckle]

513
00:19:57,822 --> 00:19:59,865
I'm so sorry.
I know nothing about this.

514
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,451
That's why Janine wanted
to meet with you.

515
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,121
You didn't want me to speak.

516
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,373
You wouldn't listen to me.

517
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,125
You won't let me speak.

518
00:20:09,542 --> 00:20:10,710
You never listen.

519
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,294
You never let me speak.

520
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:14,088
You never let me speak!

521
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:16,716
You never ever let me speak!
[whimpers]

522
00:20:16,799 --> 00:20:19,176
[shouting] Never! How crazy is that?

523
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,595
Are you screaming at me?

524
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:23,139
Yes, ma'am, I am screaming at you!

525
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:24,640
I can't take this job anymore!

526
00:20:24,724 --> 00:20:26,851
No. I can't do this. I hate this!

527
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,394
I can't do this anymore!

528
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,979
No more of this, my god!

529
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,689
I can't do this anymore!

530
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,065
[in English] Oh, my god, Ms. Andrea!

531
00:20:33,149 --> 00:20:35,276
I quit! I quit!

532
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,319
I... [pants]

533
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:42,032
Wait. I'll handle this.
Give me a second.

534
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:44,785
[Andrea in Filipino] Look, Abi,
it's just the way I talk.

535
00:20:44,869 --> 00:20:45,995
You should be used to that by now.

536
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:47,997
We've been together for ages,
you're still this sensitive?

537
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,166
I've only been here
for two months, Ms. Andrea!

538
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,500
All the more reason to stay!

539
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:52,877
You have much more to learn from me!

540
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,628
There's so much more I can teach you!

541
00:20:54,712 --> 00:20:56,464
And you graduated
Mass Communications, right?

542
00:20:56,547 --> 00:20:59,842
I majored in Communication Research,
but there's nothing like that here!

543
00:21:00,468 --> 00:21:01,635
[Addy shouts] Out of the way!

544
00:21:02,887 --> 00:21:03,888
[Andrea] Abi!

545
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:07,516
I was 160lbs when I started here!

546
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,268
Look at how thin I've become!

547
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:11,896
Oh, my god, you have to be grateful.
You were 160lbs.

548
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:13,773
You look way better thin!

549
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:14,899
You should be thanking me.

550
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:16,400
- Abi, you can't leave...
- [Addy] Addy!

551
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,652
My name is Addy, not Abi!

552
00:21:18,736 --> 00:21:20,154
- It's Addy!
- Abi suits you better!

553
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,697
My name is Adelaida del Monte!

554
00:21:21,781 --> 00:21:24,533
You can't quit! My talents need you.

555
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:26,911
- They need you on their projects!
- [Addy] Just find someone else.

556
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,329
[Andrea] You can't go!

557
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:29,413
Who will take care of them?

558
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:32,082
You know their schedules!
You handle all their schedules!

559
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:35,419
If you resign from this office,
I'll make sure no one hires you.

560
00:21:35,503 --> 00:21:36,670
I will make sure of that.

561
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:38,464
- [Addy] Okay!
- [Andrea] Once you leave this office

562
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,299
- no company will hire you!
- [Addy] Okay!

563
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,218
- I'll make your life a living hell!
- Okay, I get it!

564
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:43,344
Okay, go ahead!

565
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,970
[in English] You ungrateful girl!

566
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:46,430
[in Filipino] I feel better now!

567
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:48,682
Fuck!

568
00:21:48,766 --> 00:21:49,767
[exhales sharply]

569
00:21:50,518 --> 00:21:53,229
Okay, please get me an appointment
with Janine Gutierrez.

570
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:54,980
Anytime she's available today,
I'm okay.

571
00:21:55,064 --> 00:21:56,273
Why me? What happened with Addy?

572
00:21:57,483 --> 00:21:58,484
She resigned, remember?

573
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,694
[Andrea] Find me
another road manager.

574
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:03,155
Ms. Andrea, that's your fourth one.

575
00:22:03,239 --> 00:22:06,283
I don't know anyone else to hire.

576
00:22:06,784 --> 00:22:07,827
Excuse me.

577
00:22:07,910 --> 00:22:09,829
[Sofie] Didn't I already
give your ID back?

578
00:22:09,912 --> 00:22:11,038
Me. You can hire me.

579
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:13,833
I'm sorry, who are you?

580
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,084
Camille.

581
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,252
[Sofie] Are you sure, miss?

582
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,711
First job?

583
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:20,172
I interned at Cinemalaya.

584
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:21,507
I studied Mass Communication.

585
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:23,634
Are you a sleepyhead?

586
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:25,302
Not really.

587
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:28,264
Good. I handle 16 celebrities.

588
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:29,765
Eight of them are big stars.

589
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:32,560
Three of them are medium,
two rising, three character actors.

590
00:22:32,643 --> 00:22:34,270
You'll be their road manager.

591
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,022
Road manager?

592
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:39,692
Road manager, yes.

593
00:22:40,109 --> 00:22:41,569
Meaning, you'll be with them on set

594
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:44,238
because you know their schedules.

595
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,824
You have to make sure
they'll come on set on time

596
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:49,201
and that they've memorized
all their lines.

597
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:52,621
If someone messes with your talents,
you mess with them.

598
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:54,456
You take the blows and the bruises.

599
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:55,708
Never the talent.

600
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:58,836
You see that coffee shop over there?
That one, see that?

601
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:00,588
You'll get my coffee there
every morning.

602
00:23:00,671 --> 00:23:02,798
[in English] My coffee
is an organic decaf soy latte.

603
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:03,883
Please remember that.

604
00:23:03,966 --> 00:23:05,467
[in Filipino]
If your shooting location

605
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:06,552
is anywhere near here

606
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:08,679
you'll get your talent's orders
there too.

607
00:23:08,762 --> 00:23:10,723
Everything they want, get it there.

608
00:23:11,307 --> 00:23:14,727
You make sure their taxes
are filled out and paid.

609
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:17,062
- Got it.
- If a fan wants a picture

610
00:23:17,146 --> 00:23:20,733
you take the camera, the phone,
or whatever gadget it is.

611
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:23,777
Make sure the talent is clearly seen,
and it's the correct angle.

612
00:23:23,861 --> 00:23:25,154
It's fine if the fans' faces
are blurry.

613
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:26,238
Okay.

614
00:23:26,322 --> 00:23:27,781
If the talent farts, take the blame.

615
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:29,575
You go to the producer
and collect their fees.

616
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:31,368
Manicures and pedicures
are very important.

617
00:23:31,452 --> 00:23:32,995
The talent's nails
should always be clean.

618
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:34,914
Dirty nails are bad for their image.

619
00:23:35,289 --> 00:23:36,749
A foot spa is a must.

620
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:39,960
If they also need hair and makeup,
then go and do it, I don't care.

621
00:23:40,044 --> 00:23:44,340
In short, you represent me
and Shine Artist Management.

622
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:45,424
Can you do it?

623
00:23:47,468 --> 00:23:49,053
- Can you?
- I can.

624
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:54,975
Am I hired?

625
00:23:57,019 --> 00:23:58,437
You're a Mass Communication
graduate, right?

626
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,272
- What's your major?
- [Camille] Film.

627
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:23,170
Gab, I'm an old man.

628
00:24:23,253 --> 00:24:24,880
[Samuel] You're making me dizzy.

629
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:29,760
Sorry, boss.
I just don't know what to do.

630
00:24:30,219 --> 00:24:32,346
[Gab] Matthew's right, it's one movie

631
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:33,806
but she'll be a star overnight.

632
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,225
She could be set for life with this.

633
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:37,559
But...

634
00:24:37,810 --> 00:24:39,645
Am I the only one who feels sorry?

635
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:41,355
[in English]
It seems like everything's happening

636
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,648
so fast for her, and...

637
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:43,857
Seriously?

638
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:45,609
Breast augmentation?

639
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:47,861
[in Filipino] I trust you'll make
the right choice, Gab.

640
00:24:51,073 --> 00:24:52,366
That's it?

641
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:54,743
No words of wisdom?

642
00:24:55,703 --> 00:24:57,496
- No advice?
- Huh?

643
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:00,541
Gab, will you sit down?

644
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:02,084
Relax! Sit.

645
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:05,004
What advice can I give someone

646
00:25:05,087 --> 00:25:07,339
who is almost just like me?

647
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:10,551
You know everything I know.

648
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:12,094
There's nothing left to teach you.

649
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:16,265
The one thing I can't teach you
is the gut feel.

650
00:25:17,433 --> 00:25:20,519
Everything you need
is in that brain of yours.

651
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:25,065
Whatever your heart tells you,
you have to figure that out.

652
00:25:26,108 --> 00:25:28,610
I taught you everything,
how to play the game.

653
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:30,946
The rest is up to you.

654
00:25:35,826 --> 00:25:36,827
Shit!

655
00:25:37,578 --> 00:25:39,788
[Samuel] Do you see it clearly now?

656
00:25:40,748 --> 00:25:42,583
I have to go. See you later!

657
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:44,668
[somber music]

658
00:25:50,591 --> 00:25:52,134
Excuse me.

659
00:25:55,137 --> 00:25:57,139
[background chatter]

660
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:07,733
[background chatter continues]

661
00:26:15,491 --> 00:26:16,533
[Gab] Lora!

662
00:26:16,617 --> 00:26:18,869
Lora? I'm not Lora!

663
00:26:18,952 --> 00:26:19,953
Sorry!

664
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:21,330
Hello!

665
00:26:21,622 --> 00:26:23,040
[Lora over phone] I'm driving.

666
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:25,250
Uh... I'm here.

667
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:27,795
[Lora] Your son and I already left.

668
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,756
Can I talk to Joey?

669
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:32,591
[Lora] He's napping. I need to go.

670
00:26:32,674 --> 00:26:34,802
The cops will see me on the phone.

671
00:26:34,885 --> 00:26:38,180
- Wait! Can't you wake him up for me?
- [dial tone beeps]

672
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:40,599
Hello?

673
00:26:40,682 --> 00:26:42,810
[upbeat music]

674
00:26:44,812 --> 00:26:46,563
[Chin] Administrative departments
are on this floor.

675
00:26:46,647 --> 00:26:50,109
HR, Accounting, Library, Procurement.

676
00:26:50,192 --> 00:26:52,778
Okay, and here's the lobby.

677
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:54,196
Come on, quickly!

678
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:57,366
There's the one
who refused to let you in.

679
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:59,576
- You've met Sofie, of course?
- [Sofie] Yes.

680
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:01,578
This is our photocopy area.

681
00:27:01,662 --> 00:27:03,831
'Cause, you know,
photocopying is life.

682
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:08,585
This is our main conference room,
where we do all our meetings.

683
00:27:08,669 --> 00:27:10,587
- Even me?
- Of course!

684
00:27:10,671 --> 00:27:13,215
Road managers attend meetings.

685
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,467
- [hammer thudding]
- You were here earlier, right?

686
00:27:15,551 --> 00:27:17,136
This is where you had your interview.

687
00:27:17,219 --> 00:27:18,220
[Chin] Wait.

688
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:21,014
This is Deo, our maintenance man.

689
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:22,307
Deo!

690
00:27:22,975 --> 00:27:24,643
Please check the lamp
in Sir Gab's room.

691
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:27,604
It keeps winking at me
like it wants me.

692
00:27:27,688 --> 00:27:28,772
Have a look at it, okay?

693
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,774
Thank you!

694
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:32,484
[in English] And this.

695
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:36,697
This is the heart
of Shine Artist Management.

696
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:44,955
[in Filipino] Here is
the most exciting department at SAM.

697
00:27:47,332 --> 00:27:48,959
You've met Andrea, of course.

698
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:52,754
You're her road manager. Good luck.

699
00:27:53,547 --> 00:27:55,591
That's Gabriel, my boss.

700
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:57,634
He's a bit preoccupied these days.

701
00:27:58,177 --> 00:27:59,553
He just separated from his wife.

702
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:03,390
You'll meet Matthew soon,
he's just busy.

703
00:28:03,473 --> 00:28:04,600
He's a senior manager too.

704
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:08,604
That one is Noemi, his road manager.

705
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,649
[Chin in English]
I saved the best for last.

706
00:28:13,859 --> 00:28:14,860
Oh!

707
00:28:15,903 --> 00:28:17,696
Welcome to the pantry!

708
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:18,989
[Daisy] Were you able to heat that?

709
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:21,241
[in Filipino] Let's wait here
for other people you haven't met.

710
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,035
[Chin] Keep this pantry
close to your heart.

711
00:28:23,327 --> 00:28:24,369
Starting tomorrow

712
00:28:24,453 --> 00:28:28,373
you'll have breakfast here, lunch,
snacks, dinner, even midnight snacks.

713
00:28:28,624 --> 00:28:29,791
That is, if you're not on set.

714
00:28:30,459 --> 00:28:33,795
Hey, don't forget
the fish you ordered.

715
00:28:33,879 --> 00:28:35,255
Is that still fresh, Miss Daisy?

716
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:37,257
Fresher than you, girl!

717
00:28:37,341 --> 00:28:39,843
And here you are, trespassing again.

718
00:28:39,927 --> 00:28:41,261
You don't even work here!

719
00:28:41,345 --> 00:28:43,722
Anyway, here's your tablet.

720
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:46,391
Everything's already there,
your username and password.

721
00:28:46,475 --> 00:28:48,727
All the artists and celebrities

722
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:50,562
under Shine Artist Management
are listed there

723
00:28:50,646 --> 00:28:53,315
as well as
their senior managers, okay?

724
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:57,694
Names, contact info, addresses,
contact sheets. It's all there.

725
00:28:57,778 --> 00:29:00,197
Explore and study it, okay, Camille?

726
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,323
Any questions?

727
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,033
- Not really.
- Okay.

728
00:29:03,116 --> 00:29:04,201
Thank you, Chin!

729
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:05,285
See you tomorrow!

730
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:06,912
You mean I can go home now?

731
00:29:10,624 --> 00:29:11,792
Sis?

732
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,795
Enjoy it
while the answer's still "yes".

733
00:29:15,212 --> 00:29:17,923
When you get home,
call everyone dear to you

734
00:29:18,006 --> 00:29:19,341
because starting tomorrow

735
00:29:19,424 --> 00:29:20,592
your days will be longer.

736
00:29:20,676 --> 00:29:22,010
You'll live here now.

737
00:29:24,012 --> 00:29:26,431
[in English]
Welcome to Shine Artist Management!

738
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:53,709
[telephone rings]

739
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:56,628
Hello.

740
00:29:57,212 --> 00:29:58,213
Where?

741
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:00,257
Hello?

742
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:05,637
[thuds]

743
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:19,067
Sofie?

744
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:21,570
Sofie?

745
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:24,364
[in Filipino] Where is everyone?

746
00:30:28,869 --> 00:30:30,871
[cell phone vibrating]

747
00:30:31,163 --> 00:30:32,205
[gasps]

748
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:34,291
What do I tell Sir Samuel?

749
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:36,251
Didn't you tell him where to go?

750
00:30:36,335 --> 00:30:38,003
- No.
- You idiot!

751
00:30:38,086 --> 00:30:39,463
- Hey!
- [Sofie] My phone!

752
00:30:39,963 --> 00:30:40,964
[Sofie gasps]

753
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:43,800
[cell phone vibrating continues]

754
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:47,095
[Gab] Quickly!

755
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:48,680
[Andrea] Give her phone back.

756
00:30:48,764 --> 00:30:49,765
[Gab] Here you go.

757
00:30:50,307 --> 00:30:51,308
- He's here...
- [gasps]

758
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:53,477
What's all this?

759
00:30:53,769 --> 00:30:57,522
[in unison] Surprise!

760
00:30:57,606 --> 00:30:59,608
[calm music]

761
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:06,907
We can't let you leave
without a send-off, Samuel!

762
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:08,492
- Of course.
- A send-off?

763
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:10,160
I'll only be gone for two weeks!

764
00:31:10,744 --> 00:31:12,496
To make you look even more handsome.

765
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:14,164
- Wow!
- Thank you!

766
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:15,248
Looks good!

767
00:31:15,332 --> 00:31:17,501
- Looks good!
- Looks good. Thank you, Noemi.

768
00:31:18,085 --> 00:31:19,461
- This is for you.
- Thank you, everyone.

769
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:21,546
[cheering]

770
00:31:23,131 --> 00:31:24,216
[sighs]

771
00:31:25,509 --> 00:31:27,427
You know... [clears throat]

772
00:31:27,511 --> 00:31:29,763
...people always say

773
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:31,973
I'm the heart of SAM.

774
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:33,850
[Samuel] But that's not true.

775
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:38,605
Part of my job is to teach you

776
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:43,151
everything I know
about this industry.

777
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:48,115
My biggest source of pride

778
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:51,118
is that I picked
the right people to teach.

779
00:31:52,035 --> 00:31:55,414
You're the heart
of Shine Artist Management.

780
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:57,249
[in Filipino] Don't ever forget that.

781
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:00,460
- [Gab] Yes, boss.
- Okay.

782
00:32:00,544 --> 00:32:02,629
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

783
00:32:02,712 --> 00:32:03,964
There's more to say

784
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:06,383
but I'll save the rest
for my retirement.

785
00:32:06,466 --> 00:32:07,884
[all laugh]

786
00:32:07,968 --> 00:32:10,762
Just keep on working
on those projects

787
00:32:10,846 --> 00:32:12,472
especially Juan Makabayan!

788
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:13,890
- [Andrea] Juan Makabayan.
- Okay.

789
00:32:13,974 --> 00:32:17,769
[Samuel] And no fighting
while I'm away, okay?

790
00:32:17,853 --> 00:32:19,438
[overlapping dialogue]

791
00:32:19,521 --> 00:32:21,314
See you in two weeks. Okay.

792
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:22,941
- See you!
- Cheers!

793
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,025
[camera shutter clicks]

794
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:25,527
[overlapping dialogue]

795
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,446
[employee] Love you, boss! Love you!

796
00:32:27,988 --> 00:32:29,990
[comical music]

797
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,284
Sir, I need one last signature.

798
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:33,952
- You barely made it!
- Please, sir?

799
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,287
Maybe you should sign it?

800
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:36,413
Only you can do it, sir.

801
00:32:37,247 --> 00:32:38,248
There you go.

802
00:32:38,331 --> 00:32:40,250
- Okay.
- Thank you, sir, love you!

803
00:32:40,834 --> 00:32:42,335
Samuel, I...

804
00:32:42,419 --> 00:32:44,421
I just want to apologize for earlier.

805
00:32:44,504 --> 00:32:46,381
[in English]
It's totally uncalled for.

806
00:32:46,465 --> 00:32:47,799
I'm so sorry.

807
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:52,637
[in Filipino]
Look, I get how passionate you are.

808
00:32:54,097 --> 00:32:57,017
But you put too much pressure
on yourself

809
00:32:57,100 --> 00:32:59,686
that you take it out on others.

810
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:02,522
Take a breath. Okay?

811
00:33:03,273 --> 00:33:04,316
[in English] Relax.

812
00:33:04,524 --> 00:33:05,817
Yeah, I'll take note of that.

813
00:33:05,901 --> 00:33:06,943
Take care of yourself, okay?

814
00:33:07,027 --> 00:33:08,069
- You too.
- Okay.

815
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:10,030
- Have fun.
- [in Filipino] And you, Gab.

816
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,531
- Remember everything I said.
- Okay.

817
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:17,662
Samuel.

818
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:21,791
[in English]
Don't worry about Juan Makabayan.

819
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:23,376
[in Filipino] I'll handle it.

820
00:33:23,835 --> 00:33:25,253
[in English] We've come far, Matthew.

821
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:30,300
[in Filipino] SAM would not be SAM
if I didn't convince you to join me.

822
00:33:30,383 --> 00:33:31,384
[in English] Thank you.

823
00:33:32,469 --> 00:33:33,970
[in Filipino] I want you to know that

824
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:36,515
it's you that I trust the most.

825
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:39,476
Um...

826
00:33:39,559 --> 00:33:40,852
Don't make any decisions

827
00:33:41,311 --> 00:33:42,562
until I get back.

828
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:44,481
Um...

829
00:33:45,065 --> 00:33:46,066
[in English] What do you mean?

830
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:47,484
[in Filipino]
We'll talk when I get back.

831
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:48,860
Take care.

832
00:33:49,611 --> 00:33:50,612
You too.

833
00:33:51,905 --> 00:33:52,948
[in English] Have fun!

834
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:55,408
- We'll miss you, boss!
- [in Filipino] Take care!

835
00:33:55,492 --> 00:33:57,494
[dramatic music]

836
00:34:04,584 --> 00:34:06,461
Hello. Good evening.

837
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,799
- [roommate 1] Did you eat already?
- [roommate 2] Have some dinner.

838
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:12,717
[Camille] I'll go unpack first.

839
00:34:12,801 --> 00:34:13,927
Thank you.

840
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:16,054
- Hello.
- Hi.

841
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:17,180
That's your bed.

842
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:18,431
Okay. Thank you.

843
00:34:21,351 --> 00:34:23,353
[cell phone vibrating]

844
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:34,322
Hello, Mom.

845
00:34:38,785 --> 00:34:39,828
[in English] Guess what?

846
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:44,291
[in Filipino] Margie, I can't fight
that soap opera about schedules!

847
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:46,918
They said it's down
to the last two episodes.

848
00:34:47,002 --> 00:34:49,588
Don't believe them. Check again.

849
00:34:50,213 --> 00:34:52,132
Cel? Pull up the file for the budget.

850
00:34:52,215 --> 00:34:53,967
Yes, Mother, hang on.

851
00:34:54,926 --> 00:34:58,847
Rey, my piano is still out of tune!

852
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:02,267
I just finished tuning it, Mother.

853
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:04,227
Mother, here is the maquette.

854
00:35:04,311 --> 00:35:06,062
Okay, it's nice.

855
00:35:06,813 --> 00:35:08,023
- [yelps]
- How about this, Mother?

856
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:09,941
Let me hear it.

857
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:12,110
- [piano plays]
- There you go.

858
00:35:12,986 --> 00:35:15,030
[exclaims] Too high!

859
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,573
The budget?

860
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:18,825
Not you, Cel. I mean Rey.

861
00:35:19,034 --> 00:35:20,619
[Aleta] It's too high!

862
00:35:20,702 --> 00:35:21,703
How much?

863
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:23,371
We agreed on 20,000.

864
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:25,915
[prop maker]
This is 25,000, 15,000, and 5,000.

865
00:35:25,999 --> 00:35:27,917
Twenty thousand? That's too high!

866
00:35:28,001 --> 00:35:30,086
Mother, here it is.

867
00:35:30,170 --> 00:35:32,047
The finest toilet bowl we have.

868
00:35:32,339 --> 00:35:33,548
- I don't like the color.
- [gasps]

869
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:34,966
Do it again. Try it again.

870
00:35:35,050 --> 00:35:37,010
[piano plays high key]

871
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,803
It's still too high.

872
00:35:38,887 --> 00:35:41,556
Change it.
We won't even see that on screen.

873
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,350
This is a night scene, right?

874
00:35:43,642 --> 00:35:44,893
Let's go with the 5,000.

875
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:47,062
- [prop maker] And this?
- [Aleta] Very good.

876
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:49,439
But I get a discount.
It's only one eye.

877
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:52,317
Mother, you were right.

878
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:56,196
They still have two weeks left
on that soap opera.

879
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:59,074
I told you so. Replace it!

880
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,283
The entire piano?

881
00:36:00,367 --> 00:36:01,868
Not you, Rey!

882
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:05,413
Margie, give me the list

883
00:36:05,497 --> 00:36:06,790
of everyone you will replace.

884
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:08,041
That's all good.

885
00:36:08,458 --> 00:36:09,709
The tune?

886
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:11,336
No, Rey. No.

887
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,754
Cel, for the budget

888
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:14,881
- it's all good to me.
- Yes, ma'am.

889
00:36:14,964 --> 00:36:19,177
Rey! Do not leave
until that piano is tuned, okay?

890
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,261
Okay.

891
00:36:20,345 --> 00:36:21,554
Okay. Bye.

892
00:36:23,765 --> 00:36:24,766
[exhales sharply]

893
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:26,851
[comical music]

894
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,398
[server] Here you go, Mother.

895
00:36:32,899 --> 00:36:35,026
I spend a lot of money here every day

896
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:36,528
so this dessert should be free, okay?

897
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:38,363
- Yes, Mother.
- Okay.

898
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:40,156
And you, mister?

899
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:41,700
[Niño] Mother.

900
00:36:41,783 --> 00:36:43,702
All they give me are father roles.

901
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:45,620
I'm too young for that.

902
00:36:46,121 --> 00:36:47,872
So what do you want?

903
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:50,166
Do you wanna be in a love team?

904
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:51,751
A rom-com?

905
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:53,211
I'm serious, Mother.

906
00:36:54,462 --> 00:36:55,463
Niño.

907
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:57,465
Stop asking me for all these things.

908
00:36:57,549 --> 00:36:59,217
I already gave you stardom.

909
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:04,556
Your comeback is in SAM's hands now.

910
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:10,770
Mother, is that guy from SAM too?

911
00:37:13,857 --> 00:37:15,859
[inaudible dialogue]

912
00:37:15,942 --> 00:37:17,360
That's Paul Amir.

913
00:37:18,278 --> 00:37:19,362
He's not from SAM.

914
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:22,198
He's from Galaxy Entertainment.

915
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:25,452
Hi!

916
00:37:26,870 --> 00:37:27,912
Hi!

917
00:37:28,538 --> 00:37:29,539
Hi!

918
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:31,916
[in English] How are you?

919
00:37:37,922 --> 00:37:40,091
[tense music]

920
00:37:44,429 --> 00:37:45,430
[Sofie] Thank you!

921
00:37:48,183 --> 00:37:49,809
[Andrea in Filipino] Sofie, a favor?

922
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:53,813
- [thuds]
- Sofie!

923
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:58,193
Ms. Andrea, please watch my play.

924
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:00,945
- [Sofie] Take Sir Gab with you.
- Sure.

925
00:38:01,029 --> 00:38:03,823
- [Andrea] Sure.
- Okay then, Ms. Andrea.

926
00:38:04,073 --> 00:38:05,158
- Okay?
- What can I do for you?

927
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:06,242
Okay, good.

928
00:38:06,326 --> 00:38:09,996
[in English] Please send Cassie
a beautiful bouquet of flowers.

929
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:13,041
[in Filipino] And an order
of her favorite nachos.

930
00:38:13,124 --> 00:38:15,960
Then add a very cute and lovely note.

931
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:17,879
Something like, "I love you forever."

932
00:38:18,463 --> 00:38:20,465
Or if you think of something better.

933
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:21,883
You kids would know what to say.

934
00:38:22,175 --> 00:38:23,176
Uh...

935
00:38:24,761 --> 00:38:25,762
Yes?

936
00:38:26,387 --> 00:38:28,389
Which Cassie, Ms. Andrea?

937
00:38:28,473 --> 00:38:30,266
Cassie, my girlfriend. Who else?

938
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:34,813
The new girl can't do this.
She hasn't even met Cassie.

939
00:38:34,896 --> 00:38:37,106
[in English]
So please, can you do it for me?

940
00:38:43,196 --> 00:38:44,197
[in Filipino] Seriously?

941
00:38:44,614 --> 00:38:45,615
Here.

942
00:38:54,207 --> 00:38:56,251
WHY, WHAT HAPPENED?

943
00:38:59,128 --> 00:39:01,130
[cell phone vibrating]

944
00:39:02,215 --> 00:39:03,216
[exhales sharply]

945
00:39:04,509 --> 00:39:05,510
[scoffs]

946
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:07,804
[Cassie over phone] Andrea.

947
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:08,888
Babe!

948
00:39:09,597 --> 00:39:10,974
[Cassie in English]
Stop calling me that.

949
00:39:11,683 --> 00:39:13,059
Wait! [scoffs]

950
00:39:13,142 --> 00:39:16,646
[in Filipino] What did I do?
Why are you so angry?

951
00:39:17,146 --> 00:39:19,232
[Cassie] We're done talking.

952
00:39:19,774 --> 00:39:21,317
I've been telling you for weeks.

953
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:22,485
I want out.

954
00:39:22,569 --> 00:39:23,903
[Andrea] Is this about my workload?

955
00:39:23,987 --> 00:39:25,280
[in Filipino] I can cut back on work.

956
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,865
[in English]
You know what, I could give...

957
00:39:28,950 --> 00:39:32,370
Some of my talents
to Gab, to Matty, and...

958
00:39:32,453 --> 00:39:33,997
So we can spend more time together!

959
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:35,748
[in Filipino]
That's what you want, right?

960
00:39:35,832 --> 00:39:37,041
No!

961
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:39,544
My god, you're not listening again.

962
00:39:39,627 --> 00:39:40,628
[in English] Amazing!

963
00:39:40,837 --> 00:39:42,171
[Andrea] Wait, babe. Please.

964
00:39:42,255 --> 00:39:43,381
[in Filipino] Stop being angry.

965
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:45,341
[in English]
Just tell me what you want.

966
00:39:45,425 --> 00:39:46,801
[in Filipino] What I want

967
00:39:46,885 --> 00:39:49,679
- is for you to get a life, Andrea.
- [video call wavering]

968
00:39:49,762 --> 00:39:51,222
- You're suf...
- Shit! The signal.

969
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:53,558
[video call wavering]

970
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:56,227
- I know this is harsh, but...
- [yells] Signal!

971
00:39:56,311 --> 00:39:58,771
What? Why do you say I smother you?

972
00:39:58,855 --> 00:40:00,648
[in English]
I give everything you want, Cassie.

973
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:02,233
What are you talking about?

974
00:40:02,525 --> 00:40:03,735
[Cassie in Filipino] That's just it.

975
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:06,070
You like everything I like.

976
00:40:06,446 --> 00:40:08,114
[in English]
My hobbies, the food that I eat.

977
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:09,657
Even my hair!

978
00:40:09,741 --> 00:40:12,201
It's like you're trying to be me.

979
00:40:12,285 --> 00:40:14,078
- [car horn honks]
- Wait!

980
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:16,289
[in Filipino] Not you... I mean...

981
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:17,749
Fine, go ahead!

982
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:20,168
I thought that would make you happy.

983
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:23,129
[Cassie] You're allergic to garlic,
but you eat it because I love garlic.

984
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:26,090
You hate jazz,
but you go to concerts with me.

985
00:40:26,174 --> 00:40:30,178
You couldn't care less about Lego,
but now you're a collector.

986
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:34,223
Isn't it good
that I make adjustments for you?

987
00:40:34,307 --> 00:40:35,725
Definitely not!

988
00:40:35,808 --> 00:40:38,102
Ms. Andrea! You're not allowed there.

989
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:43,274
I'm not allowed here.

990
00:40:43,358 --> 00:40:44,442
[mouths] Wait.

991
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:46,861
Fine, I'm leaving.

992
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:48,112
I hate my life.

993
00:40:49,072 --> 00:40:50,448
[in English] Cassie, I'm sorry.

994
00:40:51,532 --> 00:40:52,575
I'm sorry.

995
00:40:52,659 --> 00:40:55,453
[in Filipino] Your entire world
can't revolve around me, Andrea.

996
00:40:55,995 --> 00:40:58,289
It's not healthy for you or for me.

997
00:41:00,792 --> 00:41:02,669
[in English] I just love you so much.

998
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:05,964
I just love you so much. [sobs]

999
00:41:06,047 --> 00:41:07,882
[Cassie in Filipino]
I know I'm the only one you love.

1000
00:41:07,966 --> 00:41:10,551
But I can't be the only one you like.

1001
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:13,429
I'm not a bad person, Andrea.

1002
00:41:14,013 --> 00:41:16,891
I would never ask my girlfriend
to make those sacrifices.

1003
00:41:16,975 --> 00:41:18,017
I don't need it.

1004
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:21,145
[in English]
I don't know who you are anymore.

1005
00:41:22,313 --> 00:41:23,439
[in Filipino] You're so fake.

1006
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:25,984
[in English] Look, I promise.

1007
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:28,111
I promise I can change.

1008
00:41:28,194 --> 00:41:29,237
Good.

1009
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,155
[in Filipino] Do that for your sake.

1010
00:41:32,115 --> 00:41:34,951
But you'll have to do it alone
because I'm done.

1011
00:41:36,244 --> 00:41:37,286
[in English] Goodbye, Andrea.

1012
00:41:38,413 --> 00:41:40,415
[sobbing]

1013
00:41:46,379 --> 00:41:48,381
[sobbing continues]

1014
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:55,722
[in Filipino] Stupid Cassie.

1015
00:41:55,805 --> 00:41:57,015
It's just Cassie.

1016
00:41:58,433 --> 00:42:00,435
[sobbing]

1017
00:42:02,061 --> 00:42:04,063
[sobbing continues]

1018
00:42:07,150 --> 00:42:09,652
[breathes deeply]

1019
00:42:11,154 --> 00:42:12,613
There's plenty
of other women out there.

1020
00:42:13,364 --> 00:42:14,907
With legs longer than hers.

1021
00:42:15,074 --> 00:42:16,993
[quivers]

1022
00:42:18,494 --> 00:42:19,662
[exhales sharply]

1023
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:23,374
[exhales]

1024
00:42:26,044 --> 00:42:27,336
[in English] I hate you, Cassie.

1025
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:29,881
Okay.

1026
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:33,134
[door closes]

1027
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:37,930
[toilet flushes]

1028
00:42:44,353 --> 00:42:45,855
Uh...

1029
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:47,273
[in English]
Let's start this meeting!

1030
00:42:49,025 --> 00:42:50,610
[in Filipino] Where's my RM
and what's her name?

1031
00:42:50,693 --> 00:42:51,694
It's Camille.

1032
00:42:51,778 --> 00:42:52,945
- And where's Camille?
- Right here.

1033
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:56,866
Get me a meeting with Janine now.

1034
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:01,037
Isn't it too early for a meltdown?

1035
00:43:02,163 --> 00:43:03,873
Sir Gab, this is Camille.

1036
00:43:03,956 --> 00:43:05,291
Ms. Andrea's new RM.

1037
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:07,460
- Hi, Camille.
- Hello, sir.

1038
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:09,253
Do you guys have
Janine Gutierrez's number?

1039
00:43:10,630 --> 00:43:11,964
[all in unison] Tablet.

1040
00:43:13,049 --> 00:43:14,217
Go ahead. Test it.

1041
00:43:15,093 --> 00:43:16,385
Test it... No, wait.

1042
00:43:16,469 --> 00:43:19,138
There, I see blood. That's enough.

1043
00:43:19,222 --> 00:43:21,682
[Aleta] I'm buying the blood.

1044
00:43:21,766 --> 00:43:22,850
Okay, we're done.

1045
00:43:22,934 --> 00:43:24,102
Don't forget the cost breakdown.

1046
00:43:24,185 --> 00:43:25,603
- [seller] Okay, ma'am.
- [Matthew] Mother.

1047
00:43:25,686 --> 00:43:26,729
Another meeting?

1048
00:43:26,813 --> 00:43:28,731
- Matthew!
- Mm-hm.

1049
00:43:28,815 --> 00:43:29,857
Thanks.

1050
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:32,985
How about you?

1051
00:43:33,653 --> 00:43:35,029
Another meeting?

1052
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:38,116
What, you mean last time?

1053
00:43:38,199 --> 00:43:40,034
No, that wasn't a meeting.

1054
00:43:40,326 --> 00:43:42,245
Paul and I are old golfing buddies.

1055
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:43,454
We were just catching up.

1056
00:43:43,538 --> 00:43:44,539
Mmm...

1057
00:43:44,831 --> 00:43:48,000
Even when I was just a manager in SAM

1058
00:43:48,459 --> 00:43:50,002
I've always held my meetings here.

1059
00:43:51,129 --> 00:43:52,171
So I've heard.

1060
00:43:52,505 --> 00:43:54,340
It's almost like you own the place.

1061
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:55,675
[Aleta chuckles] Agree.

1062
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:59,595
[in English] This is the place
where deals are made

1063
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:01,180
and dreams are broken.

1064
00:44:01,889 --> 00:44:03,766
[in Filipino]
This was where I told Samuel

1065
00:44:03,850 --> 00:44:05,309
that I was leaving SAM

1066
00:44:05,601 --> 00:44:06,811
to become a producer.

1067
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:09,814
Really? Samuel never told me that.

1068
00:44:09,897 --> 00:44:11,774
I can't admit it

1069
00:44:12,942 --> 00:44:14,944
but I really do favor SAM.

1070
00:44:15,862 --> 00:44:18,281
I spent some of my best years there.

1071
00:44:18,948 --> 00:44:22,743
I saw Samuel's hard work
to make a star out of SAM.

1072
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:27,957
If something bad ever happens to SAM

1073
00:44:29,417 --> 00:44:31,711
like Samuel, it would hurt me too.

1074
00:44:37,550 --> 00:44:38,551
Kiray.

1075
00:44:38,634 --> 00:44:40,052
So you've heard the good news.

1076
00:44:40,303 --> 00:44:42,930
[Gab] Congratulations, they love you!

1077
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:46,642
They want a Filipino actor for
Women in Chains, and they want you.

1078
00:44:46,726 --> 00:44:50,229
I had to learn
from a casting agent friend

1079
00:44:50,313 --> 00:44:51,647
that I didn't get the part.

1080
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:54,233
You know what,
I just found out myself

1081
00:44:54,317 --> 00:44:55,484
that Kiray got it.

1082
00:44:56,027 --> 00:44:59,363
But still, honey, it's not
a good reason for you to leave SAM.

1083
00:44:59,447 --> 00:45:02,158
Thanks God!

1084
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:04,577
But Kiray needs
breast augmentation surgery.

1085
00:45:05,036 --> 00:45:06,037
What?

1086
00:45:06,454 --> 00:45:08,372
Wait. Is that in the contract?

1087
00:45:08,456 --> 00:45:09,916
Not yet, but they'll add it in.

1088
00:45:09,999 --> 00:45:11,375
She'll have to get the surgery.

1089
00:45:11,459 --> 00:45:12,668
And if we refuse?

1090
00:45:12,752 --> 00:45:14,712
They loved your audition!
It was beautiful.

1091
00:45:14,795 --> 00:45:15,922
I saw it and I agree.

1092
00:45:16,005 --> 00:45:17,298
[Andrea] You were so good.

1093
00:45:17,381 --> 00:45:19,759
But no one told me
why I didn't get it.

1094
00:45:20,343 --> 00:45:23,596
Hello, Pappy? Get here right away!

1095
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:25,348
They'll blow up our baby's boobs!

1096
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:28,351
[in English] It's just that,
according to them

1097
00:45:28,684 --> 00:45:33,481
you were a bit on the mature side.

1098
00:45:33,564 --> 00:45:34,607
Mature?

1099
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:36,108
[Janine] Seriously?

1100
00:45:36,359 --> 00:45:37,777
[in Filipino] "Mature" as in "old"?

1101
00:45:37,860 --> 00:45:40,404
Maybe they'll still grow some more.

1102
00:45:41,072 --> 00:45:42,448
I'm only 18 years old.

1103
00:45:42,907 --> 00:45:43,950
- Twenty-one.
- Twenty-one.

1104
00:45:44,033 --> 00:45:45,910
[in English] Andrea, I'm only 26!

1105
00:45:45,993 --> 00:45:47,411
Twenty-six?

1106
00:45:48,663 --> 00:45:50,039
You look 20 to me.

1107
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:54,085
[in Filipino] Gabriel, we agreed
to change her showbiz age to 21

1108
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:56,587
to get her bigger and better roles.

1109
00:45:56,671 --> 00:45:58,422
Now she needs showbiz boobs too?

1110
00:45:58,506 --> 00:46:00,341
But the role

1111
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:03,928
requires you to be
a bit more mature and hot.

1112
00:46:04,011 --> 00:46:05,429
So what's the problem, then?

1113
00:46:05,513 --> 00:46:06,973
Asking price?

1114
00:46:07,056 --> 00:46:08,724
Hot? How about this?

1115
00:46:10,184 --> 00:46:11,769
Why didn't you fight for me?

1116
00:46:11,978 --> 00:46:13,479
Janine, of course I did!

1117
00:46:13,562 --> 00:46:15,856
I would never abandon my talents!

1118
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,608
[in English] And, sweetheart,
I love you so much!

1119
00:46:17,692 --> 00:46:19,318
You know I'll do everything for you!

1120
00:46:19,777 --> 00:46:21,070
[in Filipino] But...

1121
00:46:22,947 --> 00:46:24,323
You wouldn't lower your rate

1122
00:46:25,783 --> 00:46:27,368
so that's two points against us.

1123
00:46:28,536 --> 00:46:30,746
[Andrea] You shouldn't have done
those mother roles.

1124
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:32,373
[in English] Oh, my god.

1125
00:46:32,456 --> 00:46:35,042
Andrea, this is unbelievable!

1126
00:46:35,334 --> 00:46:37,128
[in Filipino]
I'm almost the same age as Kiray!

1127
00:46:37,211 --> 00:46:39,588
[Janine] And for the record,
she looks older than me!

1128
00:46:39,672 --> 00:46:41,340
She looks like my older sister!

1129
00:46:41,424 --> 00:46:44,051
[Gab] That's what I told
the casting agent.

1130
00:46:44,135 --> 00:46:45,761
Maybe you can use a costume instead?

1131
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:48,889
And I'm scared
of any kind of surgery.

1132
00:46:48,973 --> 00:46:49,974
Okay!

1133
00:46:50,057 --> 00:46:51,642
So we're passing on the project.

1134
00:46:51,726 --> 00:46:54,270
We can find more projects
for you here.

1135
00:46:54,353 --> 00:46:56,439
And even internationally.

1136
00:46:56,522 --> 00:46:59,317
We can make paid social media content

1137
00:46:59,400 --> 00:47:00,943
for advertising.

1138
00:47:01,277 --> 00:47:03,279
I'll make you a social media star!

1139
00:47:04,530 --> 00:47:06,991
We'll get
that 150,000-dollar talent fee

1140
00:47:07,074 --> 00:47:08,784
somewhere else!

1141
00:47:08,868 --> 00:47:10,661
One hundred and fifty thousand...

1142
00:47:11,412 --> 00:47:13,622
US dollars?

1143
00:47:13,706 --> 00:47:14,790
Exactly!

1144
00:47:15,082 --> 00:47:20,171
So you're saying the older I get,
the less expensive I should be?

1145
00:47:20,546 --> 00:47:22,882
[in English]
For that role and for that project?

1146
00:47:22,965 --> 00:47:24,091
Multiplied by 60.

1147
00:47:27,928 --> 00:47:28,971
Hello, Pappy?

1148
00:47:29,055 --> 00:47:30,389
[in Filipino] You don't need to come.

1149
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:31,974
We'll talk later.

1150
00:47:32,433 --> 00:47:36,937
And tell Didi she can now go
to school in France.

1151
00:47:37,813 --> 00:47:39,732
Her sister is making a new movie!

1152
00:47:39,815 --> 00:47:42,109
Ask me where!

1153
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:45,363
In Holy Wood! [squeals]

1154
00:47:45,696 --> 00:47:47,656
[in English] But look, Janine.

1155
00:47:47,740 --> 00:47:49,492
- Oh, my god.
- [Andrea] There are more better

1156
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:50,951
and bigger roles for you.

1157
00:47:51,035 --> 00:47:53,746
You're a very talented star.
You're beautiful. You're young.

1158
00:47:53,954 --> 00:47:56,207
[in Filipino]
There's so much we can do together!

1159
00:47:56,290 --> 00:47:57,833
You and I, I promise you that!

1160
00:48:01,420 --> 00:48:02,880
They are kind of tiny.

1161
00:48:02,963 --> 00:48:05,132
[Mrs. Celis]
It's for your career, baby!

1162
00:48:05,216 --> 00:48:06,592
Let's look at it this way.

1163
00:48:06,675 --> 00:48:09,762
Your future will be brighter

1164
00:48:10,638 --> 00:48:13,224
if your boobs are bigger.

1165
00:48:13,307 --> 00:48:15,059
If you can't do your job

1166
00:48:15,142 --> 00:48:19,230
then I'll go to an agency
that can do the job for me.

1167
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:21,315
[retreating footsteps]

1168
00:48:25,069 --> 00:48:26,487
Hi!

1169
00:48:27,196 --> 00:48:28,447
[Kiray] Hey, Janine!

1170
00:48:28,823 --> 00:48:29,949
How are you?

1171
00:48:31,575 --> 00:48:33,786
[in English] I'll be okay. Soon!

1172
00:48:35,871 --> 00:48:38,040
So fresh! See you around!

1173
00:48:40,835 --> 00:48:41,919
[sighs]

1174
00:48:50,428 --> 00:48:52,221
Before anything else

1175
00:48:52,304 --> 00:48:54,932
if anyone comes in,
what's the safe word?

1176
00:48:55,516 --> 00:48:56,559
- "Volleyball."
- "Volleyball."

1177
00:48:56,642 --> 00:48:57,935
Very good, children!

1178
00:48:58,018 --> 00:48:59,145
Okay, what else?

1179
00:48:59,937 --> 00:49:00,938
That's it.

1180
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:03,274
After she was dumped, the call ended

1181
00:49:03,858 --> 00:49:05,151
and she just sobbed.

1182
00:49:05,860 --> 00:49:07,403
[Chin] Poor Ms. Andrea.

1183
00:49:07,653 --> 00:49:10,948
Serves her right
for being such a jerk.

1184
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:14,076
Hey, she's going through a lot.

1185
00:49:14,410 --> 00:49:16,328
I've worked here the longest.

1186
00:49:16,412 --> 00:49:17,455
I know that she's kind...

1187
00:49:17,538 --> 00:49:18,998
Volleyball!

1188
00:49:19,081 --> 00:49:20,082
[clears throat]

1189
00:49:20,166 --> 00:49:22,084
- [Noemi] She's a kind player!
- [Chin] Right.

1190
00:49:22,168 --> 00:49:23,794
- I always watch her play.
- [Sofie] Me too.

1191
00:49:23,878 --> 00:49:25,963
- A "kind" player?
- Yes, kind.

1192
00:49:26,046 --> 00:49:27,089
How can a player play kindly?

1193
00:49:29,258 --> 00:49:33,179
- She's kind to her opponents.
- [Sofie] We all agree.

1194
00:49:33,262 --> 00:49:36,891
We just have to accept the fact that

1195
00:49:36,974 --> 00:49:39,268
she can be a mean player sometimes.

1196
00:49:39,602 --> 00:49:40,603
[gasps]

1197
00:49:40,895 --> 00:49:42,813
[Daisy] Yeah, that's how it is.

1198
00:49:43,272 --> 00:49:45,524
That player, I mean.

1199
00:49:47,109 --> 00:49:48,277
- Do you agree?
- [Sofie] Yes.

1200
00:49:48,360 --> 00:49:50,070
You have time for gossip, huh?

1201
00:49:50,154 --> 00:49:51,947
Be quick, we have lots of work to do.

1202
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:54,283
- [Chin] Yes, ma'am.
- [Sofie] Yes, ma'am.

1203
00:49:54,366 --> 00:49:56,076
- [Noemi] Yes, ma'am.
- [Camille] Yes, ma'am.

1204
00:49:56,160 --> 00:49:58,329
All clear, she's gone.

1205
00:49:58,412 --> 00:49:59,497
Here's more.

1206
00:49:59,955 --> 00:50:01,999
You know Ms. Andrea.

1207
00:50:02,583 --> 00:50:03,667
She's a film major.

1208
00:50:03,751 --> 00:50:06,128
She's intense and driven.

1209
00:50:06,212 --> 00:50:07,588
That's just how she is.

1210
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:10,216
[Sofie] With work
and her love life too.

1211
00:50:10,299 --> 00:50:12,676
So heartbreaks are also so intense.

1212
00:50:12,760 --> 00:50:13,761
[Chin] Too bad.

1213
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:18,015
You know,
I still haven't met Sir Matthew.

1214
00:50:18,349 --> 00:50:19,892
- Is he a good boss?
- [Daisy exclaims]

1215
00:50:19,975 --> 00:50:24,688
Of course! Good and good-looking!

1216
00:50:24,772 --> 00:50:27,816
- Sir Matthew is so macho!
- [Sofie] Sir Matthew is so macho!

1217
00:50:27,900 --> 00:50:30,152
[Noemi] Are you making fun
of Sir Matthew?

1218
00:50:30,236 --> 00:50:33,531
Noemi wouldn't last here
if Sir Matt wasn't a good boss.

1219
00:50:34,114 --> 00:50:36,575
For me, he's the best.

1220
00:50:36,742 --> 00:50:38,452
He manages

1221
00:50:38,536 --> 00:50:40,704
the biggest talents in SAM.

1222
00:50:40,788 --> 00:50:41,872
[Noemi] That's how good he is.

1223
00:50:41,956 --> 00:50:43,207
[Daisy] Look how proud she is!

1224
00:50:43,290 --> 00:50:44,416
[Chin] Very proud.

1225
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:48,170
Right. He's not a film major

1226
00:50:48,254 --> 00:50:50,923
but it seems he knows
what's best for his talents.

1227
00:50:52,341 --> 00:50:53,551
He's a business graduate.

1228
00:50:54,802 --> 00:50:57,721
How did you know
he wasn't a film major?

1229
00:51:00,432 --> 00:51:01,767
[Sofie] Wait a minute.

1230
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,435
I've been wondering about something.

1231
00:51:03,519 --> 00:51:05,271
You say you don't know Sir Matthew.

1232
00:51:05,354 --> 00:51:06,647
But when you first got here

1233
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:09,441
you asked specifically
for Sir Matthew.

1234
00:51:10,985 --> 00:51:12,236
I read it on the website!

1235
00:51:13,320 --> 00:51:14,530
The website!

1236
00:51:14,613 --> 00:51:16,699
[Camille] I wanted to work here.

1237
00:51:16,782 --> 00:51:18,367
I saw his name on the website.

1238
00:51:18,450 --> 00:51:20,452
[playful music]

1239
00:51:23,455 --> 00:51:25,374
Can you just stick to Ms. Andrea?

1240
00:51:25,457 --> 00:51:27,334
- [Chin exclaims]
- Because Sir Matthew is mine.

1241
00:51:27,418 --> 00:51:30,546
- Oh! Yours? Like you own him?
- [Chin gasps]

1242
00:51:30,629 --> 00:51:32,131
[Noemi] It's not like that!

1243
00:51:32,214 --> 00:51:33,299
[laughs]

1244
00:51:33,382 --> 00:51:36,135
Did she change her name to "Hope"?

1245
00:51:36,427 --> 00:51:38,929
Just give up on Sir Matthew.

1246
00:51:39,013 --> 00:51:40,889
How about Sir Gab? He's single now.

1247
00:51:40,973 --> 00:51:42,391
- Ms. Andrea too.
- [Chin] I'll set you up.

1248
00:51:42,474 --> 00:51:44,059
You think that will work?

1249
00:51:44,768 --> 00:51:48,564
Seriously, I really don't know
how to help Ms. Andrea.

1250
00:51:50,649 --> 00:51:52,735
[line ringing]

1251
00:51:52,818 --> 00:51:55,404
Come on, Cassie! Pick up!

1252
00:51:56,405 --> 00:51:57,573
Where are you?

1253
00:51:58,157 --> 00:52:00,159
[Gab] Just give Cassie
the space she wants.

1254
00:52:00,242 --> 00:52:02,578
She's right.
You do smother her sometimes.

1255
00:52:02,786 --> 00:52:03,787
[Andrea] Excuse me.

1256
00:52:04,330 --> 00:52:05,664
I know how to compromise.

1257
00:52:05,748 --> 00:52:08,876
But how can I show her that

1258
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:10,336
if she won't even speak to me?

1259
00:52:10,794 --> 00:52:12,630
She won't even take my calls.

1260
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:16,425
And do you mind
not taking her side today?

1261
00:52:16,508 --> 00:52:17,718
It's all too fresh.

1262
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:19,136
[sighs]

1263
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:21,347
[in English] I just miss her so much.

1264
00:52:22,890 --> 00:52:24,475
[in Filipino] I miss Joey too.

1265
00:52:24,975 --> 00:52:26,977
[somber music]

1266
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:40,199
Camille.

1267
00:52:40,866 --> 00:52:42,493
[in English]
I told you not to come back here.

1268
00:52:42,576 --> 00:52:43,619
[in Filipino] Wait.

1269
00:52:45,204 --> 00:52:46,789
I can give you a monthly allowance.

1270
00:52:46,872 --> 00:52:48,415
Just give me your bank details.

1271
00:52:53,379 --> 00:52:56,090
No one knows
I have a daughter out of wedlock.

1272
00:52:59,551 --> 00:53:00,678
This will ruin me.

1273
00:53:02,179 --> 00:53:03,347
[Andrea] Oh, you're here!

1274
00:53:03,430 --> 00:53:05,015
[in English]
Anyway, I need you to do something.

1275
00:53:05,099 --> 00:53:06,975
Leave this in my office, okay? And...

1276
00:53:07,059 --> 00:53:08,519
[in Filipino]
Do you two know each other?

1277
00:53:09,645 --> 00:53:10,646
- Not at all.
- Oh, not yet.

1278
00:53:10,896 --> 00:53:12,523
Matthew Buenaventura,
our senior manager.

1279
00:53:12,606 --> 00:53:14,483
- This is Francine...
- Camille Vergara.

1280
00:53:15,317 --> 00:53:17,861
Camille Francine Vergara.
My new road manager.

1281
