Did you get it? Did you like it?

1535
01:04:04,799 --> 01:04:07,510
Why would you give me a hand mirror?

1536
01:04:09,387 --> 01:04:11,264
[Janine in Filipino]
To remind me that I'm too old

1537
01:04:11,348 --> 01:04:13,350
for the biggest role of my career?

1538
01:04:13,433 --> 01:04:15,101
[in English] But that's vintage!

1539
01:04:15,185 --> 01:04:17,270
[Janine scoffs] Apparently, so am I.

1540
01:04:18,521 --> 01:04:21,816
- [exhales sharply]
- Look. I appreciate it. Okay?

1541
01:04:23,276 --> 01:04:24,319
[in Filipino] Maybe...

1542
01:04:24,944 --> 01:04:26,404
I'm just sensitive right now.

1543
01:04:27,489 --> 01:04:28,907
But you really should be too.

1544
01:04:29,282 --> 01:04:31,117
Anyway, it's a good thing you called

1545
01:04:31,201 --> 01:04:32,786
because I wanted to tell you

1546
01:04:33,078 --> 01:04:35,789
I'm thinking of signing
with Paul Amir of Galaxy.

1547
01:04:36,706 --> 01:04:39,250
[in English]
So I guess this is goodbye.

1548
01:04:40,085 --> 01:04:41,211
Thanks, Andrea.

1549
01:04:48,259 --> 01:04:49,260
You're fired.

1550
01:04:49,677 --> 01:04:50,887
Get out of my office.

1551
01:04:52,597 --> 01:04:53,598
Get out!

1552
01:04:57,894 --> 01:04:59,229
- [in Filipino] Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

1553
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:01,189
- What happened?
- I'm okay.

1554
01:05:01,272 --> 01:05:03,274
[indistinct chatter]

1555
01:05:04,734 --> 01:05:05,735
[sighs]

1556
01:05:11,241 --> 01:05:12,283
[in English] Look.

1557
01:05:12,992 --> 01:05:14,077
Okay, you're not fired.

1558
01:05:14,160 --> 01:05:15,286
Ms. Andrea, I'm sorry.

1559
01:05:17,580 --> 01:05:19,374
[in Filipino]
I know things can get tough here.

1560
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:21,751
Especially since it's your first day.

1561
01:05:22,419 --> 01:05:23,420
So stop crying.

1562
01:05:24,129 --> 01:05:26,131
It's gonna get worse.

1563
01:05:26,714 --> 01:05:28,299
So don't waste your tears on this.

1564
01:05:29,259 --> 01:05:30,260
What's the problem?

1565
01:05:30,760 --> 01:05:31,803
[in English] Well...

1566
01:05:33,471 --> 01:05:37,892
Janine suddenly decided
that she's finally out of SAM.

1567
01:05:37,976 --> 01:05:41,146
[in Filipino]
So, SAM just lost Janine Gutierrez.

1568
01:05:41,813 --> 01:05:44,441
Well, then let's look
for another Janine.

1569
01:05:45,191 --> 01:05:47,193
Come on, I'll buy you a drink.

1570
01:05:47,527 --> 01:05:49,195
Let's drown your worries in alcohol.

1571
01:05:49,279 --> 01:05:50,572
Me? I'm celebrating.

1572
01:05:50,989 --> 01:05:52,615
What's there to celebrate?

1573
01:05:53,575 --> 01:05:54,826
I feel relieved.

1574
01:05:54,909 --> 01:05:58,037
I've decided to pass on
Women In Chains for Kiray.

1575
01:05:58,121 --> 01:05:59,164
What?

1576
01:05:59,247 --> 01:06:01,666
Oh, my god,
you should have decided sooner!

1577
01:06:02,125 --> 01:06:05,044
You know, because maybe if you did

1578
01:06:05,587 --> 01:06:08,715
I could have gotten Janine that part
and maybe she would still be in SAM.

1579
01:06:10,758 --> 01:06:11,759
Excuse me.

1580
01:06:13,178 --> 01:06:14,471
Are you out of your minds?

1581
01:06:15,889 --> 01:06:17,390
[in English]
Do you realize how much money

1582
01:06:17,474 --> 01:06:18,808
we could have made from that film?

1583
01:06:20,685 --> 01:06:22,729
Samuel said it was up to me.

1584
01:06:22,812 --> 01:06:24,105
[in Filipino]
And that's what I decided.

1585
01:06:24,564 --> 01:06:26,149
I can live with losing that project

1586
01:06:26,232 --> 01:06:28,985
than have my talent
go through that surgery.

1587
01:06:29,277 --> 01:06:30,737
Besides, I already told Kelly.

1588
01:06:30,820 --> 01:06:31,905
End of conversation.

1589
01:06:31,988 --> 01:06:34,199
- Let's go, Andrea.
- Let's go. I agree.

1590
01:06:34,282 --> 01:06:35,325
Excuse me.

1591
01:06:38,578 --> 01:06:40,455
Excuse me, Ms. Manuel.

1592
01:06:40,538 --> 01:06:41,664
Can you explain

1593
01:06:42,081 --> 01:06:43,917
why you let Janine leave SAM?

1594
01:06:44,125 --> 01:06:46,503
You let her leave, now it's possible
she'll head to our biggest rival.

1595
01:06:46,586 --> 01:06:48,463
[in English]
I don't have to explain to you.

1596
01:06:48,546 --> 01:06:49,547
What?

1597
01:06:50,173 --> 01:06:52,509
[in Filipino] Do you realize
what you've done to SAM?

1598
01:06:52,967 --> 01:06:56,054
It's not like
we're not doing our jobs.

1599
01:06:58,097 --> 01:07:00,517
You call that "doing your jobs"?

1600
01:07:01,267 --> 01:07:02,810
[Matthew] You passed on
what could have been

1601
01:07:02,894 --> 01:07:05,063
the biggest break
of your talent's career.

1602
01:07:05,563 --> 01:07:07,857
Can you please just let it go, okay?

1603
01:07:08,066 --> 01:07:10,735
The project's gone.
Janine left already.

1604
01:07:10,818 --> 01:07:13,238
- Just... Just get off of our backs!
- [telephone rings]

1605
01:07:13,488 --> 01:07:16,449
Why don't you just focus
all your energy on Niño Muhlach?

1606
01:07:16,533 --> 01:07:18,618
You seem to be a good match.

1607
01:07:18,701 --> 01:07:20,328
Focus on finding projects for him!

1608
01:07:20,411 --> 01:07:21,412
Stay away from us!

1609
01:07:21,621 --> 01:07:23,831
Maybe he can go audition
for Hollywood.

1610
01:07:23,915 --> 01:07:25,250
So we can still keep that project.

1611
01:07:25,333 --> 01:07:26,543
[in unison] Get the phone!

1612
01:07:27,085 --> 01:07:29,254
[telephone ringing]

1613
01:07:32,674 --> 01:07:34,551
[in English] Shine Artist Management,
how may I help you?

1614
01:07:34,634 --> 01:07:36,052
[Andrea] You can't tell us
what to do.

1615
01:07:36,135 --> 01:07:38,221
- I don't care about what they say.
- Yes.

1616
01:07:38,888 --> 01:07:40,181
Mind your own talents.

1617
01:07:40,265 --> 01:07:41,474
I'll mind my own.

1618
01:07:41,558 --> 01:07:42,559
Ms. Andrea?

1619
01:07:42,642 --> 01:07:44,644
[clamoring]

1620
01:07:44,727 --> 01:07:45,770
[Sofie] Sir Gabriel?

1621
01:07:45,853 --> 01:07:46,980
It can't always be about you!

1622
01:07:47,647 --> 01:07:48,815
Sir Matthew?

1623
01:07:48,898 --> 01:07:50,775
[Andrea] You always find fault
in what we do.

1624
01:07:50,858 --> 01:07:52,026
You know, we can grow, too!

1625
01:07:52,110 --> 01:07:53,111
[shushes]

1626
01:07:53,611 --> 01:07:54,654
[in unison] What?

1627
01:07:55,822 --> 01:07:56,948
It's Sir Samuel.

1628
01:07:57,323 --> 01:07:58,324
Oh...

1629
01:08:03,538 --> 01:08:05,290
Hey, Samuel. Uh...

1630
01:08:05,957 --> 01:08:07,083
We're all here!

1631
01:08:07,417 --> 01:08:09,377
You miss us already, boss?

1632
01:08:09,627 --> 01:08:11,254
[in English] How's everything?
Are you having fun?

1633
01:08:11,546 --> 01:08:14,007
[doctor] Sorry,
this is not Samuel Mendiola.

1634
01:08:14,173 --> 01:08:16,426
I'm calling from Avalon Clinic
in Germany.

1635
01:08:19,053 --> 01:08:20,179
What's this about?

1636
01:08:20,763 --> 01:08:22,140
I'm sorry to tell you this.

1637
01:08:22,390 --> 01:08:23,933
Mr. Samuel Mendiola suffered

1638
01:08:24,017 --> 01:08:26,144
a massive heart attack
late last night.

1639
01:08:28,980 --> 01:08:30,023
How is he?

1640
01:08:30,106 --> 01:08:31,733
He passed away about an hour ago.

1641
01:08:36,362 --> 01:08:38,364
[foreboding music]

1642
01:08:39,699 --> 01:08:40,700
Yes, hello.

1643
01:08:41,159 --> 01:08:44,287
This is Matthew Buenaventura,
associate of Samuel.

1644
01:08:46,706 --> 01:08:48,416
- [electricity crackles]
- [loud thud]

1645
01:08:49,834 --> 01:08:51,836
[closing theme music]
